# Example witness for circuit/reanchoring_recursion_spike/src/main.nr (N=4,
# a fixed-size, pre-padding-redesign snapshot of the header-chain logic, kept
# frozen for this recursion feasibility spike's own measurements -- NOT kept
# in sync with circuit/reanchoring/src/main.nr's later changes).
#
# This is the SAME fixture as this circuit's own valid_chain_satisfies_circuit
# test (src/main.nr); verified via a real `nargo test` + `nargo execute` pass
# this session. Its hash_header is a 2-round Poseidon2 SPONGE (absorbs 4
# inputs, IV encodes length) -- an EARLIER design than the deployed
# circuit/reanchoring/src/main.nr, which now uses the raw single-call
# std::hash::poseidon2_permutation (see that circuit's own Prover.toml.example
# and circuit/README.md's "Poseidon2 Verification History"). The two crates'
# hash_header outputs do NOT match for the same header anymore -- don't copy
# values between the two examples.
#
# To use: cp Prover.toml.example Prover.toml, then
# `bb prove --verifier_target noir-recursive` (this leaf is proven with the
# recursive target, not the default one -- see circuit/README.md §2).

